# std.uuid — random UUID generation, declared in Chezzi (phase 4e).
#
# FILE-BACKED, IMPORT-GATED native module (same pattern as std/regex.chz). Its functions are in scope
# ONLY after `import std.uuid` (or an `import … from std.uuid`). The resolver loads this real file
# (keeping the `native` marker), and the checker harvests the `native fn` declarations below as the
# module's SIGNATURE source — retiring the hand-built `native_module_sig` uuid arm.
#
# Every declaration is BODY-LESS: the implementations stay native (name-keyed in `src/native/uuid.rs`,
# dispatched via `native_members("std.uuid")`).

# `v4()` → a fresh random UUID str. By DEFAULT it draws 16 bytes from the OS CSPRNG per call (the same
# source as crypto.secure_bytes, the same shape as CPython's uuid.uuid4) — unpredictable, no PRNG
# state, fails closed if the OS can't supply entropy.
native fn v4() -> str
# `uuid_seed(n)` OPTS OUT of that: it switches v4() to a reproducible 64-bit SplitMix64 stream for
# golden runs. The switch is process-global and STICKY (no way back), and that stream is PREDICTABLE
# from one observed UUID — never call it in a program whose ids are tokens or session ids.
native fn uuid_seed(n: int) -> nil
